WEBVTT

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:04.140
When can a higher payoff rate
hide repayment risk?

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:08.930
I tested the same 25,000
simulated businesses,

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.680
with repayment tied to daily sales.

00:00:12.165 --> 00:00:14.815
On AWS, I used PowerShell

00:00:14.855 --> 00:00:17.945
to open an early version
of the campaign console.

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:20.885
In the browser, I submitted the campaign

00:00:20.925 --> 00:00:24.495
for 25,000 merchants
and watched its progress.

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:29.970
50,000 decisions and over half a million
daily monitoring records

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:33.720
took 15 hours and 26 minutes
of computation.

00:00:34.302 --> 00:00:39.342
Tableau shows 3,337 businesses
funded in Baseline.

00:00:39.972 --> 00:00:44.062
Under Recession Energy,
1,005 receive financing.

00:00:44.798 --> 00:00:50.088
At day 120, about 5.3%
still owed money in Baseline.

00:00:50.578 --> 00:00:53.848
Under stress, only 4.3% did.

00:00:54.445 --> 00:00:58.755
Now follow the 1,005 businesses
funded both times.

00:00:59.255 --> 00:01:02.065
36 still owed money in Baseline,

00:01:02.545 --> 00:01:04.595
43 under stress.

00:01:05.277 --> 00:01:06.537
Why the reversal?

00:01:07.257 --> 00:01:09.707
140 open Baseline accounts

00:01:09.747 --> 00:01:14.607
belonged to businesses that received
no financing under stress.

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:17.990
In Power BI, we see this restaurant

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:21.670
received $150,000 both times.

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:25.810
The same share of eligible daily sales
went toward repayment.

00:01:26.537 --> 00:01:28.877
Payments matched through day 60.

00:01:29.427 --> 00:01:32.617
The shock reached collections
on day 61.

00:01:33.117 --> 00:01:35.957
Baseline paid off on day 118.

00:01:36.653 --> 00:01:40.963
Under stress, it still owed about $10,700

00:01:41.003 --> 00:01:42.383
on day 120.

00:01:42.957 --> 00:01:46.387
Before expanding credit on the strength
of a payoff rate,

00:01:46.837 --> 00:01:48.997
I’d check who got funded

00:01:49.037 --> 00:01:51.477
and how those same businesses repaid.

